{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLTwHuQjwckM2FPx6W5C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #204 with status **done**: it goes to the engineer triage planner, and the **engineer** worker will implement it. The decision is in `.ard/204/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **Why it isn't blocked:** the issue said it had to wait for #215, but that work is already on main. The `route` key is in `internal/config/load.go`, including the check that stops an LLM scanner from using `pending`, and `internal/scanner/guard.go` exists.\n- **Worker scope:** the issue's own plan gives only the first of its four PRs to the worker. That PR is pure, table-tested code in `internal/config` and `internal/scanner`. PRs 2 to 4 change the executor mounts, the agent adapter and the credential path, and the plan says a human should lead them. I flagged this for maintainers.\n- **Other notes for maintainers:**\n  - The PR 4 docs change touches `CLAUDE.md`, which is protected and needs a human approval.\n  - The owner's later comment adds a change so untriaged LLM-scanner issues also go stale and get closed. The engineer planner should say which PR carries it.\n  - No architect or documentation-planner roles exist in this repo, so only `triage:engineer` is in the routing list. The only reviewer, eng-review, has no `when:` rule, so it will run on the PR without being added."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":913,"cache_read_input_tokens":37047,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":913},"output_tokens":444,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a07f3996-86e2-4c9d-9205-5f6cbc271088","uuid":"5d82f24e-8fcc-4583-a96b-abcc28a29a82","timestamp":"2026-11